@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Create a typed child or initiative
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "Opening page / WorkItemFormDialog / WorkItemForm" as page
  participant "IWorkItemService / WorkItemService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkItemsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "CreateWorkItemCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkItem" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Add from the pinned header (registered by the tab page), an empty state, a parent's row, or the detail's children card
page -> page : The page that offers Add (WorkHierarchyPage, WorkItemDetailPage, WorkListPage, BacklogPage, ProjectOverviewPage, KanbanBoardPage, or SprintBoardPage) opens WorkItemFormDialog with a WorkItemFormContext
page -> page : Preselect context.parent; the parent combobox debounces typed text about 250 ms into parentQuery (GetWorkItemsQuery for the required parent type, matching title or parent title, bounded pages), so every valid parent is reachable; a task's hint names its story's sprint
page -> page : WorkItemForm emits draftChange on every edit; the dialog and the opening page expose FormDraft
opt Cancel, Close, or Escape with a dirty draft
  page -> page : UnsavedChangesDialog asks first; Keep editing returns with every value; Discard closes and sends nothing
end
opt Assignee chosen
  page -> page : Searchable active-people combobox; see the assignee sequence in Edit, assign, and reparent work
end
actor -> page : Save the form
page -> page : Disable Save while pending (L2-031)
page -> client : Build typed CreateWorkItemCommand
client -> access : POST /api/workspaces/{id}/work-items
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401 (nothing written); sign-in shows session-unsaved when a draft was dirty, then returns to the project
else Authenticated active account (profile P: creating work needs no capability beyond an active session)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send CreateWorkItemCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-015 / L2-016 validate title 1-200, description up to 10,000, parent required by type; the command carries the type and both dates, so the validator also checks an estimate only for a story (a whole number of 0 or more) and a due date on or after the start date
  alt Invalid fields
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Keep every value; one field error moves focus to that field, which reads its error; several focus the linked error summary (validation state); no Retry or reference ID
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle CreateWorkItemCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync takes the workspace lock first; then LoadWorkItemCreationAsync (workspace, parent, tracked sibling order, and for a story the backlog order and Kanban board) and LoadAccountStatusAsync for a chosen assignee
    db --> handler : Current reference state, or lock-wait timeout
    alt Workspace lock wait times out
      handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; nothing read or changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unavailable)
      client --> page : Unavailable save, as for a 500: keep every value; alert with reference ID; focus stays on Save, which resends only when chosen (failed state)
    else Workspace not found
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : WorkItemForm emits notFound; the dialog closes with NotFound; the page calls the layout's refresh(), so the header and the view show the project's not-found state linking to Projects
    else Parent missing or deleted, wrong level, or in another workspace
      handler --> ctrl : 400 invalid parent reference; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails (parent field)
      client --> page : Keep input; remove the deleted parent from the choices; focus moves to the parent field, which reads its error; no Retry or reference ID (parent-deleted state)
    else Chosen assignee deactivated after selection, or unknown
      handler --> ctrl : 400 invalid assignee; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails (assignee field)
      client --> page : Keep the draft; focus moves to the assignee field, which reads its error; no Retry or reference ID; a new search offers active people only (rejected state)
    else References valid
      handler -> entity : L2-015 create at the level its type requires; status To Do
      entity --> handler : New work item appended after the parent's existing children
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddWorkItem and AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: insert the item, its sibling position and, for a story, its StoryBacklogPosition and To Do BoardPlacement as tracked children of the loaded orders; for a task increment the parent story's task revision only (the story's version and sprint versions unchanged); success audit; one transaction
      alt Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
        client --> page : Keep every value; alert with reference ID; focus stays on Save, which retries the same request only when chosen (failed state)
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New item ID and version; order versions incremented
        handler --> ctrl : Created item
        ctrl --> client : 201 with ID and version
        client --> page : WorkItemForm emits saved with a WorkItemSavedResult (the WorkItemSaved ID and version, the saved title, and the chosen parent's title, null for an initiative); the dialog closes with Saved(saved, title, parentTitle)
        page -> page : The opening page increments its refresh counter, so its view rereads: every expanded branch's loaded window (outline), the detail and its children, the work list page, or the backlog page
        page --> actor : The "Story added" toast (named for the item's type) through TOAST_SERVICE names the new item from title and its parent from parentTitle; focus returns to the control that opened the dialog
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the create (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The create may have committed: keep every value; the failed alert reads "We couldn't confirm whether the story was added" without a reference ID and asks to check the outline first; WorkItemForm emits unconfirmed, which the dialog relays, so the opening page increments its refresh counter and its view rereads at once; Save resends only when pressed
end
note over ctrl, db
An unexpected 403 creates nothing; WorkItemForm keeps every value and emits forbidden, WorkItemFormDialog relays it, and the routed page shows the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry or reference ID; the capability refresh still runs.
A story is appended to the story backlog and gets a Kanban BoardPlacement at the bottom of To Do in either delivery mode.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
